      "documentConcept": "Salesforce CDC custom-channel filters and field enrichment",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:137c43b63b3a8ba860abc54fa402332028e2afd7e4c2e71b487737dd34aa7088",
      "text": "Custom CDC channels select event streams with per-member filters and add unchanged context through field enrichment. For case alerting, a matching record-state predicate does not prove that the relevant field changed. Consumers must distinguish changed fields from enriched values and interpret Pub/Sub nulls using header metadata. Replayed enrichment can reflect current database values rather than the original event state. Filter syntax and field-type restrictions constrain what can be selected on the server.",
